CORE no-wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--model-stack-layout
^EXIT=1$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*--model-stack-layout requires --wide-pointer-encoding.*$
--
^VERIFICATION
--
--model-stack-layout is only meaningful together with --wide-pointer-encoding
(the stack-layout encoding is gated on wide pointers). Passing it alone must be
rejected with a usage error rather than silently doing nothing.
